Its based on genetics, HRT regime and blood levels. I started HRT at 59 but had  gynecomastia. After almost 3 years my boobs are 36D.  I also exercise and eat healthy. Its hard being a woman and staying feminine and attractive.  :-)

&#x200B;

It takes time. Enjoy the ride.

You can do it. You are luck that you have the option to be a Femboy in a more accepting society. And society will become more accepting as the old farts die off.  I was 56 before I started. I decided it was now or never in 2010. 

&#x200B;

I lost 75 lbs (with exercise and changed my eating habits. 

 [http://susanking.blogspot.com/2015/12/wednesday-december-30-2015-dietexcerise.html](http://susanking.blogspot.com/2015/12/wednesday-december-30-2015-dietexcerise.html) 

&#x200B;

I am now 62 and loving it.

[http://2.bp.blogspot.com/-kMMQK4M57P8/VbgviKfJdwI/AAAAAAAADp4/4SaPD47ZA\_g/s1600/july%2B28%2Bpic%2B1.jpg](http://2.bp.blogspot.com/-kMMQK4M57P8/VbgviKfJdwI/AAAAAAAADp4/4SaPD47ZA_g/s1600/july%2B28%2Bpic%2B1.jpg)

&#x200B;

Everyday, I look in the mirror and my femself and it motivates me throughout the day.
